Copy the base with its own copy constructor and then bulk-copy only the derived scalar tail with `memcpy`, avoiding the separate member initializations while keeping the base’s dynamic members correctly managed.

```include
#include <cstring>
```

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
{
    std::memcpy(reinterpret_cast<char*>(this) + sizeof(FieldBase),
                reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&field) + sizeof(FieldBase),
                sizeof(Field) - sizeof(FieldBase));
}
```